From bb5d9c765a9963a98472e4d92db4ce3336f6d6bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: auditor <audit@local>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 22:35:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/10] engine: observe exchange-side exits every cycle and
 book them in the ledger

INVARIANT PROTECTED: the ledger's open positions equal the venue's open
positions after every cycle. Brakes that read the ledger (open position
count, loss streak, daily loss) read something true.

Finding (audit S5, rated HIGH, certainty 100% on the first live exit):
after entry nothing in the runtime loop looked at a position again.
Stops and take-profits were venue-side orders and their fills were
observed by nothing: record_exit_fill()/close_position() were called
only by backtest.py. So positions rows lived forever, trades was never
written by a live run, MAX_CONSECUTIVE_LOSSES could never trip, and after
MAX_OPEN_POSITIONS venue-side exits the shell locked itself out of every
further entry, permanently and silently.

Thought process: the fix must (a) never place an order, (b) never invent
a position, (c) prefer venue truth for the exit price, and (d) still
book the exit when the price is unreadable, because a ledger that
disagrees with the venue about WHETHER a position exists is worse than
one with an approximate price. The approximation is labelled
(VENUE_EXIT_PRICE_UNREAD) so a human can audit it. Linear only: spot
holdings are balances, not positions, and the two must not share a path.

What changed:
  bybit_connection.py - get_closed_pnl(symbol, since_ms, limit) over
        /v5/position/closed-pnl, oldest-first, raises on failure.
  trading_engine.py   - observe_exits(): per ledger position read the venue
        size; the shortfall exited; price = qty-weighted avgExitPrice of
        closed-pnl rows newer than opened_epoch, else last price (flagged);
        books via record_exit_fill, the ONE place that decrements.
  main.py             - tick() calls observe_exits() after equity refresh and
        before should_halt_trading(), wrapped so it never kills the loop.
  tests/fake_bybit.py - serves /v5/position/closed-pnl from .closed_pnl.
  tests/test_observe_exits.py - 6 tests: spot no-op; still-open untouched;
        full stop-out booked at closed-pnl price with negative net_pnl;
        partial TP reduces qty; closed-pnl 500 still books and labels;
        no /v5/order/create is ever sent.

What did NOT change: the 5-bar HORIZON time exit of the measured rule is
still not implemented in the runtime (the runtime does not run the
measured rule at all - see patch 0002). Fee on venue exits is passed as
0.0 because closedPnl already nets fees; the ledger's net_pnl therefore
slightly overstates vs. the venue by the exit fee. Documented, not hidden.

Verification: 6/6 new tests fail on baseline. Affected suites green.
